# metric-autopsy probes — git 0b99f33, python 3.13.16, numpy 2.5.3
=================== p01_null_metrics_and_offset.py
P1a: constant metric lambda d: 0.0 on clean data, via run_autopsy defaults
  G0 DEGENERATE the metric returned the same value (0) on every resample, null and perturbation — it carries no information about the data
  G1 PASS     no confident QC imbalance in 2 assessable strata (worst point ratio 1.00x; alpha 0.05 Bonferroni)
  VERDICT: DEGENERATE METRIC — the metric returned the same value (0) on every resample, null and perturbation — it carries no information about the data

P1b: random-number metric (pure noise, no data dependence)
  G0 PASS     no bias or attenuation beyond estimator noise under any nuisance perturbation
  G1 PASS     no confident QC imbalance in 2 assessable strata (worst point ratio 1.00x; alpha 0.05 Bonferroni)
  G2 STOP     no estimand pre-registered: declare 'composition' (relative expression) or 'content' (total RNA / genes detected) — the correction depends on it
  VERDICT: UNIDENTIFIABLE — no estimand pre-registered: declare 'composition' (relative expression) or 'content' (total RNA / genes detected) — the correction depends on it

P1c: GATE 0 location-invariance: mi_3bin vs mi_3bin + C on clean data
  C=    0: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.674 z=29.9
  C=  0.5: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.674 z=29.9
  C=    1: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.674 z=29.9
  C=   10: GATE0 PASS  worst=extra_dropout rel=0.674 z=29.9

P1d: GATE 0 scale-invariance? mi_3bin * k
  k=     1: GATE0 PASS
  k=   100: GATE0 PASS
  k=  0.01: GATE0 PASS

P1e: affine reparametrisation of norm_pearson: Fisher z / (1 - r)
  r                           : GATE0 PASS worst=extra_dropout rel=0.025 base=0.520
  1-r (a 'decoupling' score)  : GATE0 PASS worst=extra_dropout rel=0.025 base=0.480
  atanh(r)                    : GATE0 PASS worst=extra_dropout rel=0.031 base=0.577
